PATCH an instance with a PatchList, as the TS client updates entities (Hylki)

The SDK updates an instance only with a whole-instance PUT, which encrypts
every value again with a fresh IV. The TS client writes every update as a
PATCH of a sys/PatchList holding only the changed, non-final attributes
(EntityRestClient.update, PatchGenerator.computePatches), so a final value
such as Mail.subject is never resent. HttpMethod gains PATCH (mapped in
NativeRestClient), EntityClient gains patch_instance, which serializes a
PatchList and PATCHes it to the instance's list element path with the
instance type's model version, mapping a non-2xx status to its HttpError
instead of panicking, and CryptoEntityClient gains a typed patch_instance
over it. An encrypted value in a patch is passed in as ciphertext: the caller
encrypts it with the instance's session key, as TS encrypts the modified
instance before computing the patch.

